<%# `x-data` (bare) opens an Alpine scope for this page. Without it Alpine never
    walks these @click bindings and the buttons are inert — silently: the page
    renders, the store exists, and every click does nothing. /lab/birthday_gate
    carries the same bare x-data for the same reason. %>
<main class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-10" x-data>
  <%# THE GLOBAL MODAL HOST, in a browser — the half of the modal system that had
      no browser coverage at all.

      /lab/birthday_gate drives `studio/modals/scoped_host` (a per-page store).
      The GLOBAL host — studio/modals/_host, the `$store.modals` singleton every
      consumer app mounts once in its layout — is a SEPARATE 800-line partial with
      its own copy of the focus trap, its own open/close/closeAllDismissible, and
      its own swap/advance animation machinery. Nothing in e2e/ ever loaded it, so
      every focus assertion in this lane graded the scoped host and the global one
      shipped on the strength of the two files looking similar.

      They are not the same file, and the seams this page exists for are exactly
      where they drifted: the scoped host said "only on a REPLACE" and the global
      host said the same thing, and both were wrong in the same way — but nothing
      would have caught it if only one had been fixed.

      THE LAB RULE (see E2eLabController): a lab page sets up a partial's LOCALS
      and nothing else. This page registers two ordinary content templates and
      three buttons; every modal behaviour under test belongs to the engine
      partial rendered by name below. %>
  <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6">Modal host (global store)</h1>

  <%# Background-page controls. They exist to be TABBED ONTO when the trap
      releases: a focus leak shows up as one of these becoming activeElement while
      a dialog is still open, which is a far sharper signal than "focus is not
      inside the dialog". %>
  <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 mb-6">
    <button type="button" data-test="open-first"
            class="btn btn-primary"
            @click="$store.modals.open('lab-first', { title: 'First card' })">
      Open first
    </button>

    <button type="button" data-test="open-second"
            class="btn btn-outline"
            @click="$store.modals.open('lab-second', { title: 'Second card' })">
      Open second
    </button>

    <button type="button" data-test="background-control" class="btn btn-outline">
      Background control
    </button>
  </div>

  <%= render "studio/modals/host" do %>
    <template x-if="$store.modals.current().id === 'lab-first'">
      <div class="p-6">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold mb-3" x-text="$store.modals.current().props.title"></h2>
        <%# TWO controls, not one: the trap's cycleFocus wraps between them, so a
            card with a single control cannot tell a working wrap from a released
            trap that happens to land back on the only focusable node. %>
        <button type="button" data-test="first-a" class="btn btn-primary">First A</button>
        <button type="button" data-test="first-b" class="btn btn-outline">First B</button>
      </div>
    </template>

    <template x-if="$store.modals.current().id === 'lab-second'">
      <div class="p-6">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold mb-3" x-text="$store.modals.current().props.title"></h2>
        <button type="button" data-test="second-a" class="btn btn-primary">Second A</button>
        <button type="button" data-test="second-b" class="btn btn-outline">Second B</button>
      </div>
    </template>
  <% end %>
</main>
